ok let's get into audience questions for  the week first one today is from Sara  Sara says hey David you've talked about  making Election Day a holiday in the  United States and that town in Ohio  actually did it  what about mail-in ballots isn't that  actually overall a better system okay so  a couple yeah it's it this is a great  idea so let's go back to what we're  trying to do the idea is for more people  to vote right now you only have in  presidential elections roughly half the  country votes sometimes it's forty five  percent fifty five percent depending on  is that a midterm is at a particularly  interesting presidential election or  whatever else that's not great I as a  progressive want as much involvement  I want people I want the country to be  as involved as possible in the process  of selecting our leaders not voting is  not a neutral act in other words when  you don't vote you're not saying I have  no influence you're saying I'm going to  have an influence in that my vote will  not be there meaning everybody else's  vote now counts a little more and I am  choosing to just allow other people to  decide that has an impact and in general  the impact is making our elected  officials in total more conservative  than the people that they represent so  we want more people to vote that's what  I want I think that would be important  we've got all the voter suppression that  we're dealing with and then on the other  side of it there are ideas about how we  might increase voter turnout one idea is  you make Election Day a holiday that  could be keeping it on Tuesday it would  be hard in the unit in the United States  to move Election Day to a different day  but in other countries they have  election days on weekends a lot of  people work on weekends so again if you  don't make it a holiday you're still  going to sort of have an issue with  people who are not going to ask for the  time off to vote because yeah you can't  get fired for going to vote but if  you're an hourly worker you're just not  going to get paid so one idea is you  make Election Day a holiday and that  helps in one way a bigger idea is you  switch to mail-in ballots and people  doesn't matter whether you work on  weekends or weekdays or whether you work  second shift or first shift or whatever  else you have some period of time  many days a couple weeks depending on  how it's set up  to fill out and send in your ballot this  is good for a number of reasons  number one it expands it's no longer  just 8 a.m. to 6 p.m. or whatever the  voting hours are during which you can  vote so if that's what was holding you  back from voting it eliminates that it  eliminates the possibility of polling  place electioneering which is another  problem that we're dealing with it  eliminates the possibility of in-person  voter suppression people coming through  lines and saying inaccurate things about  what IDs are required or scaring people  off in in some other ways that we've  covered over the last many years on the  program you deal with the possibility of  voting machines in the moment not  working you send your ballot in you fill  it out you have time to review  candidates in all of that stuff although  where the ballot is received by mail it  could still be processed by a voting  machine that could have an issue so I  think that mail-in ballots is absolutely  a fantastic idea right now you have to  request an absentee ballot if you're  going to vote by mail it has to be  approved there are only certain reasons  why you're allowed to do it although the  the strictness with which that's applied  sort of varies from state to state so I  am absolutely and completely all for it  and think it would be much better than  Election Day simply being a holiday the  issues that exist with it are all issues  because of right-wing voter suppression  we actually saw it in Georgia in the  midterm election with the gubernatorial  race you can have slick workers election  campaign workers who decide to show up  at people's houses and say I'm here to  collect the ballots and people who are  unsure about what to do or maybe don't  realize that that's crazy that you've  got to mail it they might turn over  their ballot to someone who is claiming  to be an election official but is  actually just a partisan political  operative those are the types of  problems that can come up with mail-in  ballots but that's just an awareness  thing if we put in place vote by mail  you do an awareness campaign that says  do not hand your ballot to anyone do not  do anything other than sealing the  ballot usually you put it inside of  another sometimes you put it inside of  another envelope like there's two  envelopes sometimes there isn't and mail  it that's it don't hand it to anyone  drop it in a post-office drop it off at  the post office or in a mail slot or  whatever if you know your USPS worker  okay you hand it to them because they're  actually somebody that works for the  post office that is it and we could  solve that with an awareness campaign so  I'm totally for mailing ballots I'm not  against making Election Day a holiday  but I think mail-in ballots would be  fantastic
 

